# Gate step 1176-fn2p — data, not code.
#
# Binds the fixture for build.sh's gate-memory-floor consumer: the probe's
# exit codes 0/1/3 are captured as `_mem_rc=0; _mem_out="$(…)" || _mem_rc=$?`
# and dispatched, so a floor-tier "proceed with a warning" (rc 3) no longer
# kills every macOS gate under errexit (the 2026-09-14 hotfix). Found unbound
# by 1063-nraf's reconciliation on the same day it was written; bound here.
# Hermetic: extracts the consumer block from build.sh and drives it under a
# separate bash with a stub probe; a content-built mutant dies on rc 3.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf). 2183-mfbn ported the fixture to
# Lua; its ok lines are byte-identical, so the regime pin below still quotes it.
STEP_DESC="Checking build.sh's gate-memory-floor consumer survives the probe's warning exit under errexit (1176-fn2p)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-gate-memory-floor-consumer.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the gate-memory-floor consumer regressed — a floor-tier warning would kill the gate again under errexit (1176-fn2p)"
STEP_OK="gate-memory-floor consumer holds"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:   the pre-fix capture form dies on rc 3 (rc=3), so the arm has teeth"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="build.sh scripts/check-gate-memory-floor.sh scripts/lua/test-gate-memory-floor-consumer.lua"
